From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 07:42:46 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] AP MLD: Block a scan only while a partner link scans

hostapd_driver_scan() refuses a scan with -EBUSY while a partner link of
the same AP MLD is in HAPD_IFACE_ACS, and a link stays in that state
while it waits to retry a refused scan. If a second link starts ACS
while the first one scans, its scan is refused. With acs_num_scans above
1, the next scan of the first link is then refused as well. From then on
each link finds the other in HAPD_IFACE_ACS on every retry, and both
fail after ACS_SCAN_RETRY_MAX_COUNT attempts.

The check exists because scan results without a matching scan cookie go
to the link that received the event, or to the partner links with a
scan callback. That requires at most one partner link with a scan in
progress, not at most one partner link in ACS. Test for the scan
callback instead of the interface state. The HT 20/40 MHz coexistence
scan sets the scan callback as well, so it stays covered.

Fixes: 76f8cfd6a206 ("AP MLD: Fix ACS and HT scan related issues")
Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
---

--- a/src/ap/ap_drv_ops.c
+++ b/src/ap/ap_drv_ops.c
@@ -784,7 +784,9 @@ int hostapd_driver_scan(struct hostapd_d
 
 	if (!hapd->iface->scan_cb && hapd->conf->mld_ap &&
 	    hapd->iface->interfaces) {
-		/* Other links may be waiting for scan results */
+		/* A scan event without a matching cookie goes to the partner
+		 * link that waits for scan results, so only one link at a time
+		 * can wait. */
 		unsigned int i;
 
 		for (i = 0; i < hapd->iface->interfaces->count; i++) {
@@ -799,9 +801,9 @@ int hostapd_driver_scan(struct hostapd_d
 			h_hapd = h_iface->bss[0];
 
 			if (hostapd_is_ml_partner(hapd, h_hapd) &&
-			    h_hapd->iface->state == HAPD_IFACE_ACS) {
+			    h_iface->scan_cb) {
 				wpa_printf(MSG_INFO,
-					   "ACS in progress in a partner link - try to scan later");
+					   "Scan in progress in a partner link - try to scan later");
 				return -EBUSY;
 			}
 		}
